# The porting note every behaviour change appends to. Parallel branches (worktrees, sub-agents)
# all add bullets and numbered steps to it, and a plain merge conflicts on every one of them; a
# union merge keeps both sides' lines instead. Step numbers may repeat after one — Markdown numbers
# an ordered list from its first item; tidy them when the release is cut — and CI's note check
# (release-check --unreleased) still refuses a merge that broke the frontmatter.
docs/upgrades/unreleased.md merge=union

# The Guide's committed vectors (`pnpm web guide:index`): gzipped NDJSON, so binary — no text diff,
# no line-ending conversion, and never a textual merge. On a conflict take either side and re-run
# `pnpm web guide:index` (it reuses every vector whose chunk text is unchanged). A stale file is
# harmless meanwhile: the server chunks the pages itself and borrows only vectors that still match.
apps/web/content/guide/embeddings.jsonl.gz binary
# Screenshots (`pnpm web guide:shots`) are plain PNGs, regenerated rather than merged.
apps/web/content/guide/images/*.png binary
